Subject: [PATCH] net/mlx5e: Don't store mlx5e_priv in mlx5e_dev devlink priv

commit 123eda2e5b1638e298e3a66bb1e64a8da92de5e1 upstream.

[ Backport: 6.1 has no struct mlx5e_dev (added by ee75f1fc44dd); 6.1 stores priv as auxiliary drvdata, so store the netdev there instead. ]
[ Backport: en.h unchanged; mlx5e_resume(), mlx5e_suspend_common(), mlx5e_probe() and mlx5e_remove() get netdev from drvdata and mdev from mlx5_adev. ]
[ Backport: 6.1 mlx5e_remove() has no reg_state check; unregister_netdev() takes the netdev from drvdata. ]
[ Backport: mlx5e_remove() clears the uplink netdev (CVE-2025-39947 backport) with mdev from mlx5_adev, as upstream does. ]

mlx5e_priv is an unstable structure that can be memset(0) if profile
attaching fails, mlx5e_priv in mlx5e_dev devlink private is used to
reference the netdev and mdev associated with that struct. Instead,
store netdev directly into mlx5e_dev and get mdev from the containing
mlx5_adev aux device structure.

This fixes a kernel oops in mlx5e_remove when switchdev mode fails due
to change profile failure.

